From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:17:30 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] Plutonium: the server drives the browser panel's tabs
 through Plutonium's helper

T3 Code 0.1 drives every browser tab from the server with Playwright: the
desktop app's own tabs over the desktop browser channel, everything else in
a headless Chrome that clients watch as a stream. The Plutonium shell now
takes the desktop app's part, with the browser's real tabs:

- DesktopBrowserChannel also speaks over the Plutonium helper's socket
  (GET /v1/desktop-browser, upgraded), when the server runs in a Plutonium
  session; it reconnects when the helper restarts, and is only available
  while connected (a new tab otherwise starts headless at once).
- rendersServerTabNatively: the Plutonium shell renders this server's tabs,
  as the desktop app does.
- previewBridge: createTab with a server tab hands that tab to the server
  (showServerTab in the helper's shell library); several shell pages share
  one tab. The agent's cursor arrives as pointer events, and what a page
  opens in a new tab or window opens as another tab of its thread
  (onOpenLink), as in the desktop app.
- PlutoniumBrowserHost renders server tabs as ElectronBrowserHost does.

Agents use T3's own preview tools, unchanged.

